## Leveraging `KnowledgeAISearch` — the Built-in Search Agent

Rather than building a search pipeline from scratch, codx-junior already ships a production-ready iterative AI search engine in `api/codx/junior/knowledge/knowledge_ai_search.py`. Here is how it works and how you can improve and extend it.

### How `KnowledgeAISearch` Works

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User Query] --> B[Resolve current + dependency projects]
    B --> C[Parallel Search: all projects x all queries]
    C --> D[Tag documents with project_name]
    D --> E[Filter: score > MINIMUM_SCORE_THRESHOLD]
    E --> F[Sort by score descending]
    F --> G[Keep top TOP_DOCUMENTS_LIMIT documents]
    G --> H[Merge & Deduplicate Documents]
    H --> I[AI: Is answer sufficient?]
    I -- Yes --> J[Generate Final Answer]
    I -- No --> K{Max iterations reached?}
    K -- No --> L[AI: Generate up-to-3 refined queries]
    L --> C
    K -- Yes --> J
    J --> M[Return AISearchResult with projects_searched]
```

The search uses the `Knowledge` class which wraps `KnowledgeDB` — a **Milvus BM25 full-text index** stored as a sparse vector collection. Every document returned by `Knowledge.search()` carries a `score` (BM25 relevance) in its metadata, which `KnowledgeAISearch` uses to filter and rank results across all projects in parallel.

### Using `KnowledgeAISearch` Directly

```python /home/codx-junior-projects/codx-junior/agents/run_knowledge_agent.py
import asyncio
from codx.junior.knowledge.knowledge_ai_search import KnowledgeAISearch
from codx.junior.settings import CODXJuniorSettings

async def main():
